      "content": "2.2.2 Battery Mode",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0050",
      "reading_order": 53,
      "section": "2.2.2 Battery Mode",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 77.904,
        "t": 245.69766291015628,
        "r": 541.62048,
        "b": 126.99610136319495
      },
      "content": "The working mode that battery supplies back-by power supply for the load through inverter is called battery mode. When main power fault occurs, the system will convert to battery mode automatically and the battery supplies power continuously which shall be lasted to set back-by time. Power of load is supplied by inverter output through static switch and the power of load is uninterrupted. When main power recoveries, the system will switch to main power supply mode automatically without any manual operation and power supply for load is not interrupted.  If  the back-by  time  of  battery  is overdue  but  the  main  power  still  is  not  recovered,  the  system  will  switch  to  bypass  mode automatically and uninterruptedly."
    }
